1
00:00:03,718 --> 00:00:04,886
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:04,969 --> 00:00:06,888
Earth...

3
00:00:07,013 --> 00:00:08,890
Fire...

4
00:00:09,015 --> 00:00:11,434
Air.

5
00:00:11,559 --> 00:00:12,852
Long ago...

6
00:00:12,977 --> 00:00:14,938
The four nations lived
together in harmony.

7
00:00:15,063 --> 00:00:19,984
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

8
00:00:20,109 --> 00:00:23,988
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements could stop them.

9
00:00:24,113 --> 00:00:25,782
But when the world
needed him most

10
00:00:25,907 --> 00:00:27,992
he vanished.

11
00:00:28,117 --> 00:00:31,496
100 years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

12
00:00:31,621 --> 00:00:33,456
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:33,581 --> 00:00:35,875
And although his airbending
skills were great

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,877
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:37,961 --> 00:00:39,045
AANG: Oof.

16
00:00:39,212 --> 00:00:43,091
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

17
00:00:43,216 --> 00:00:45,385
( ♪... )

18
00:00:48,012 --> 00:00:50,348
( MAN READING )

19
00:00:51,224 --> 00:00:53,393
OZAI: I am proud of you,
prince Zuko.

20
00:00:53,476 --> 00:00:56,729
I am proud because when your
loyalty was tested

21
00:00:56,854 --> 00:00:58,982
by your treacherous uncle

22
00:00:59,107 --> 00:01:00,483
you did the right thing

23
00:01:00,608 --> 00:01:02,235
and captured the traitor.

24
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:05,863
ZUKO: Why did you tell Father
that I was the one who killed the Avatar?

25
00:01:05,989 --> 00:01:07,407
Please, Zuko...

26
00:01:07,532 --> 00:01:09,617
What ulterior motive
could I have

27
00:01:09,701 --> 00:01:13,913
Unless somehow the Avatar
was actually alive?

28
00:01:13,997 --> 00:01:15,832
All that glory would
suddenly turn to shame.

29
00:01:18,876 --> 00:01:21,754
( ♪... )

30
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,001
Who's there?

31
00:02:08,801 --> 00:02:12,639
( WIND HOWLING )

32
00:02:12,722 --> 00:02:14,432
AANG: I think I see
a cave below.

33
00:02:14,515 --> 00:02:17,143
SOKKA: Shh... Keep quiet.

34
00:02:20,188 --> 00:02:21,856
( BIRD SQUAWKS )

35
00:02:21,981 --> 00:02:23,107
( APPA GRUNTS )

36
00:02:23,232 --> 00:02:26,235
Great job with the cloud camo,
but next time...

37
00:02:26,319 --> 00:02:28,071
Let's disguise ourselves as
the kind of cloud

38
00:02:28,154 --> 00:02:30,156
who knows how to keep its mouth shut.

39
00:02:30,698 --> 00:02:34,369
TOPH: Yeah, we wouldn't want a bird to
hear us chatting up there and turn us in.

40
00:02:34,494 --> 00:02:37,080
Hey, we're in enemy territory.

41
00:02:37,205 --> 00:02:39,624
Those are enemy birds.

42
00:02:39,749 --> 00:02:41,584
( SQUAWK )

43
00:02:41,709 --> 00:02:43,586
( CHUCKLING )

44
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,383
( CRASHES )

45
00:02:55,056 --> 00:02:56,641
SOKKA: Well, this is it.

46
00:02:56,724 --> 00:02:58,935
This is how we'll be living
until the invasion begins.

47
00:02:59,018 --> 00:03:01,562
Hiding in cave after cave...

48
00:03:01,646 --> 00:03:04,440
After cave after cave...

49
00:03:04,649 --> 00:03:07,735
Sokka, we don't need
to become cave people.

50
00:03:07,819 --> 00:03:09,946
What we need
is some new clothes.

51
00:03:10,029 --> 00:03:12,490
Yeah, blending in
is better than hiding out.

52
00:03:12,573 --> 00:03:14,242
If we get Fire Nation disguises

53
00:03:14,325 --> 00:03:17,620
we'll be just as safe as we
would be hiding in a cave.

54
00:03:17,704 --> 00:03:19,330
Plus, they have
real food out there.

55
00:03:19,414 --> 00:03:21,582
Does anyone wanna sit in the
dirt and eat cave-hoppers?

56
00:03:27,088 --> 00:03:29,465
( CRUNCHING )

57
00:03:29,882 --> 00:03:32,802
Looks like we
got outvoted, sport.

58
00:03:32,885 --> 00:03:34,345
Let's get some new clothes.

59
00:03:36,723 --> 00:03:38,099
AANG: I don't know about this.

60
00:03:38,182 --> 00:03:39,684
These clothes
belong to somebody.

61
00:03:39,767 --> 00:03:42,311
I call the silk robe.

62
00:03:44,981 --> 00:03:47,358
But if it's essential
to our survival

63
00:03:47,442 --> 00:03:49,610
then I call the suit.

64
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:04,333
Ta-dah... Normal kid.

65
00:04:04,751 --> 00:04:07,920
Hmm... I should
probably wear shoes

66
00:04:08,004 --> 00:04:10,590
But then I won't
be able to see as well.

67
00:04:10,923 --> 00:04:12,759
Sorry shoes...

68
00:04:15,511 --> 00:04:19,932
Finally, a stylish shoe
for the blind earthbender.

69
00:04:20,016 --> 00:04:21,392
How do I look?

70
00:04:25,855 --> 00:04:28,065
Uh, your mom's necklace.

71
00:04:28,191 --> 00:04:30,943
Oh... Oh, yeah.

72
00:04:31,068 --> 00:04:33,404
I guess it's pretty obviously
Water Tribe, isn't it?

73
00:04:46,501 --> 00:04:47,752
( MOMO PURRS )

74
00:04:50,338 --> 00:04:53,800
I used to visit my friend
Kuzon here 100 years ago.

75
00:04:53,883 --> 00:04:56,427
So everyone just follow
my lead and stay cool.

76
00:04:56,511 --> 00:04:58,304
Or as they say
in the Fire Nation

77
00:04:58,387 --> 00:05:01,390
"Stay flamin"'.

78
00:05:01,474 --> 00:05:04,018
Greetings, my good Hotman.

79
00:05:04,101 --> 00:05:05,895
Oh, hi...

80
00:05:05,978 --> 00:05:08,314
I guess?

81
00:05:08,397 --> 00:05:10,316
AANG: Oh, we're going
to a meat place?

82
00:05:10,399 --> 00:05:13,653
SOKKA: Come on, Aang,
everyone here eats meat...

83
00:05:13,736 --> 00:05:14,862
Even the meat.

84
00:05:14,946 --> 00:05:17,114
( GROWLS )

85
00:05:17,198 --> 00:05:18,533
You guys go ahead.

86
00:05:18,616 --> 00:05:20,743
I'll just get some lettuce
out of the garbage.

87
00:05:25,206 --> 00:05:27,124
AANG: Hotman, Hotman.

88
00:05:27,208 --> 00:05:29,001
Hotman.

89
00:05:29,085 --> 00:05:30,795
Hotman, Hotman.

90
00:05:31,629 --> 00:05:33,422
It's over,
we caught you.

91
00:05:33,548 --> 00:05:34,882
Who me?

92
00:05:34,966 --> 00:05:37,426
It couldn't be more obvious
that you don't belong here.

93
00:05:38,427 --> 00:05:39,679
Next time you play hooky

94
00:05:39,804 --> 00:05:42,557
You might want to take off
your school uniform.

95
00:05:43,391 --> 00:05:45,852
( NERVOUS CHUCKLE ) Ah!

96
00:05:55,319 --> 00:05:56,821
Oh...

97
00:05:56,904 --> 00:05:59,615
TEACHER: Is this a new mind
ready for molding?

98
00:05:59,699 --> 00:06:00,741
That's right.

99
00:06:00,825 --> 00:06:02,869
Let the molding begin.

100
00:06:02,952 --> 00:06:04,036
TEACHER: Wait a minute.

101
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:06,664
( GASPS ) You're not
from the Fire Nation.

102
00:06:09,542 --> 00:06:11,586
Clearly you're
from the colonies.

103
00:06:12,086 --> 00:06:15,298
Yeah, the colonies,
of course.

104
00:06:15,381 --> 00:06:18,426
The Fire Nation colonies
in the Earth Kingdom.

105
00:06:18,509 --> 00:06:20,469
Your etiquette
is terrible.

106
00:06:20,553 --> 00:06:22,430
In the homeland,
we bow to our elders...

107
00:06:23,890 --> 00:06:26,309
Like so.

108
00:06:26,392 --> 00:06:27,643
Sorry ma'am.

109
00:06:33,441 --> 00:06:36,319
And we don't wear
head coverings indoors.

110
00:06:36,402 --> 00:06:38,487
Um, I have a scar.

111
00:06:38,738 --> 00:06:40,239
It's really embarrassing.

112
00:06:40,448 --> 00:06:41,449
Very well.

113
00:06:41,532 --> 00:06:43,451
What is your name?

114
00:06:43,534 --> 00:06:47,121
Or should we just call you
mannerless colony slob?

115
00:06:47,204 --> 00:06:48,331
( CHUCKLES )

116
00:06:48,414 --> 00:06:49,874
Just "slob" is fine.

117
00:06:50,583 --> 00:06:52,501
Or, uh... Kuzon.

118
00:06:56,047 --> 00:06:57,715
( BELL TOLLS )

119
00:06:57,798 --> 00:07:01,969
( STUDENTS TALKING )

120
00:07:04,305 --> 00:07:05,306
( MOMO PURRS )

121
00:07:05,556 --> 00:07:07,183
We made it through
the day, Momo...

122
00:07:07,266 --> 00:07:08,434
And it was pretty fun.

123
00:07:08,517 --> 00:07:09,810
( PURRS )

124
00:07:09,894 --> 00:07:11,270
Don't let the headmaster
catch you with that monkey.

125
00:07:11,812 --> 00:07:13,022
What monkey?

126
00:07:13,105 --> 00:07:15,358
Don't worry,
I'm not a tattletale.

127
00:07:15,441 --> 00:07:16,442
My name's On Ji.

128
00:07:16,525 --> 00:07:18,110
I like your headband,
by the way.

129
00:07:20,071 --> 00:07:22,657
On ji, you don't have
to baby-sit the new kid.

130
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:24,575
Wow.

131
00:07:24,784 --> 00:07:27,286
You must be one of those popular
kids I've been hearing about.

132
00:07:27,495 --> 00:07:28,496
That's right.

133
00:07:28,579 --> 00:07:29,664
Now listen, friend...

134
00:07:29,747 --> 00:07:31,248
I know you're from the colonies

135
00:07:31,332 --> 00:07:32,750
so I'll say this slowly.

136
00:07:32,917 --> 00:07:36,087
On Ji is my girlfriend.

137
00:07:36,212 --> 00:07:38,047
Don't forget it.

138
00:07:44,679 --> 00:07:46,263
It was nice meeting you.

139
00:07:46,347 --> 00:07:47,473
I don't believe it.

140
00:07:47,556 --> 00:07:48,557
He didn't beat you up.

141
00:07:48,891 --> 00:07:50,142
Not even a little.

142
00:07:50,226 --> 00:07:51,811
I guess I'm just lucky.

143
00:07:51,894 --> 00:07:53,813
We were on our way to play
hide and explode.

144
00:07:53,896 --> 00:07:54,981
You wanna come?

145
00:07:55,064 --> 00:07:56,399
I'd love to.

146
00:08:01,988 --> 00:08:04,240
KATARA: Where have you been?

147
00:08:04,323 --> 00:08:05,741
We've been worried sick.

148
00:08:05,825 --> 00:08:07,576
I got invited to play
with some kids after school.

149
00:08:09,453 --> 00:08:10,746
SOKKA: After what?

150
00:08:11,122 --> 00:08:13,082
I enrolled in
a Fire Nation school

151
00:08:13,165 --> 00:08:14,583
And I'm going back tomorrow.

152
00:08:14,917 --> 00:08:17,253
Enrolled in what?

153
00:08:26,137 --> 00:08:27,221
You again?

154
00:08:27,304 --> 00:08:29,515
Stop where you are.

155
00:08:30,141 --> 00:08:32,435
GUARD: Prince Zuko?

156
00:08:32,518 --> 00:08:33,519
( SWORD CLANKS )

157
00:08:33,602 --> 00:08:34,979
Ah!

158
00:08:35,062 --> 00:08:36,731
I'm going in for a visit.

159
00:08:36,814 --> 00:08:38,149
You're gonna stand guard here

160
00:08:38,232 --> 00:08:41,444
and no one is going
to know about this.

161
00:08:50,119 --> 00:08:51,162
( DOOR CREAKS OPEN )

162
00:08:53,956 --> 00:08:56,917
Uncle... It's me.

163
00:09:07,803 --> 00:09:11,474
Aang, I'm trying to be mature and not
immediately shoot down your idea.

164
00:09:11,599 --> 00:09:14,143
But it sounds...
Really terrible.

165
00:09:14,268 --> 00:09:16,145
Yeah, we got our outfits.

166
00:09:16,270 --> 00:09:18,439
What do you need
to go to school for?

167
00:09:18,564 --> 00:09:20,441
Every minute
I'm in that classroom

168
00:09:20,566 --> 00:09:22,651
I'm learning new things
about the Fire Nation.

169
00:09:22,735 --> 00:09:24,862
I already have a picture
of Fire Lord, Ozai.

170
00:09:25,738 --> 00:09:27,615
And here's one that
I made out of noodles.

171
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:29,700
Impressive, I admit.

172
00:09:29,825 --> 00:09:31,368
But I still think
it's too dangerous.

173
00:09:31,494 --> 00:09:35,247
I guess we'll never find out
about the secret river, then.

174
00:09:35,372 --> 00:09:38,250
It goes right to
the Fire Lord's palace.

175
00:09:38,375 --> 00:09:41,253
We were supposed to learn
about it in class tomorrow...

176
00:09:41,378 --> 00:09:45,925
Hmm... I am a fan
of secret rivers.

177
00:09:46,050 --> 00:09:48,511
Fine, let's stay
a few more days.

178
00:09:48,636 --> 00:09:50,513
Flamey-O, Hotman.

179
00:09:52,765 --> 00:09:55,601
- Flamey-O?
-( SHRUGS ) Um-um.

180
00:09:57,603 --> 00:09:59,605
ZUKO: You brought this
on yourself, you know.

181
00:09:59,730 --> 00:10:01,357
We could have returned together.

182
00:10:01,482 --> 00:10:02,483
You could have been a hero.

183
00:10:04,902 --> 00:10:06,946
You had no right
to judge me, Uncle.

184
00:10:07,071 --> 00:10:09,907
I did what I had to do
in Ba Sing Se

185
00:10:10,032 --> 00:10:11,283
and you're a fool
for not joining me.

186
00:10:13,661 --> 00:10:17,248
You're not
gonna say anything?

187
00:10:17,373 --> 00:10:18,415
Oh!

188
00:10:18,541 --> 00:10:20,167
( YELLS )

189
00:10:20,292 --> 00:10:22,336
You're a crazy old man.

190
00:10:22,461 --> 00:10:24,421
You're crazy,
and if you weren't in jail

191
00:10:24,547 --> 00:10:27,174
you'd be sleeping
in a gutter.

192
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:34,557
TEACHER: Good morning, class.

193
00:10:36,225 --> 00:10:37,309
Recite the Fire Nation oath.

194
00:10:38,894 --> 00:10:41,313
STUDENTS: My life,
I give to my country.

195
00:10:41,438 --> 00:10:42,773
With my hands,
I fight for Fire Lord...

196
00:10:42,898 --> 00:10:44,567
AANG: Fire Lord...

197
00:10:44,692 --> 00:10:46,235
Forefathers...

198
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:48,612
STUDENTS: With my mind, I seek
ways to better my country

199
00:10:48,737 --> 00:10:50,281
and with my feet...

200
00:10:50,406 --> 00:10:51,490
AANG: Firebenders...

201
00:10:51,574 --> 00:10:53,367
Fire Lord.

202
00:10:53,492 --> 00:10:55,786
- Wha, bah, blah, blah.
-( STUDENTS CHUCKLING )

203
00:11:00,791 --> 00:11:04,336
Since it's obviously hilarious
to mock our national oath

204
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:07,006
we'll begin with a pop quiz on
our great march of civilization.

205
00:11:07,089 --> 00:11:09,800
( STUDENTS GROAN )

206
00:11:10,384 --> 00:11:12,428
TEACHER: Question one.

207
00:11:12,511 --> 00:11:15,306
What year did Fire Lord Sozin
battle the Air Nation army?

208
00:11:18,142 --> 00:11:19,602
Kuzon?

209
00:11:19,727 --> 00:11:21,604
AANG: Is that a trick question?

210
00:11:21,729 --> 00:11:24,773
The air nomads didn't
have a formal military.

211
00:11:24,899 --> 00:11:28,944
Sozin defeated them by ambush.

212
00:11:29,069 --> 00:11:30,738
TEACHER: Well, I don't know how you could

213
00:11:30,821 --> 00:11:32,865
possibly know more than our
national history book

214
00:11:32,990 --> 00:11:35,701
unless you were there
a hundred years ago.

215
00:11:35,826 --> 00:11:37,411
I'll just write down
my best guess.

216
00:11:42,583 --> 00:11:45,419
( ORCHESTRA PLAYS )

217
00:11:45,544 --> 00:11:48,839
( PLAYS WRONG NOTES )

218
00:11:50,716 --> 00:11:52,009
MUSIC TEACHER: Kuzon?

219
00:11:52,092 --> 00:11:53,093
( STOPS PLAYING )

220
00:11:53,177 --> 00:11:57,056
I know, I'm a terrible
tsungi hornist.

221
00:11:57,181 --> 00:11:58,224
No, child.

222
00:11:58,349 --> 00:12:00,142
That hullabaloo going
on with your feet.

223
00:12:00,267 --> 00:12:02,269
Is that a nervous disorder?

224
00:12:02,394 --> 00:12:05,105
I was just dancing.

225
00:12:05,231 --> 00:12:07,316
You do dances here in the
homeland, right?

226
00:12:07,441 --> 00:12:09,652
Not really, no.

227
00:12:09,777 --> 00:12:13,489
Dancing is not conducive to
a proper learning environment.

228
00:12:13,614 --> 00:12:16,408
Young people must have rigid
discipline and order.

229
00:12:16,533 --> 00:12:18,535
AANG: But what about
expressing yourself?

230
00:12:18,661 --> 00:12:21,372
I know sometimes we're so moved
by our love for our nation

231
00:12:21,497 --> 00:12:25,251
that we can't control
our own bodies.

232
00:12:25,376 --> 00:12:27,127
If you must

233
00:12:27,253 --> 00:12:31,882
you may march in place quietly
next time the urge hits you.

234
00:12:32,007 --> 00:12:34,843
( MUSIC RESUMES )

235
00:12:41,767 --> 00:12:46,605
( ALL TALKING/WHISPERING )

236
00:12:46,730 --> 00:12:49,275
Oh, hi, Kuzon.

237
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:51,944
I really liked that crazy
dance you were doing.

238
00:12:52,069 --> 00:12:53,153
Thanks, On Ji.

239
00:12:53,279 --> 00:12:54,780
I could show it to you
again if you'd like.

240
00:12:54,905 --> 00:12:55,948
Ah!

241
00:12:56,073 --> 00:12:57,741
What'd you say,
colony trash?

242
00:12:57,866 --> 00:12:59,535
You're gonna show her something?

243
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:01,245
Just some
dance movements.

244
00:13:01,370 --> 00:13:03,247
Nobody shows
my On Ji anything

245
00:13:03,372 --> 00:13:05,165
Especially movement.

246
00:13:05,291 --> 00:13:06,292
( GRUNTS )

247
00:13:07,710 --> 00:13:09,378
( GRUNTS )

248
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:12,423
( AUDIBLE STRUGGLING )

249
00:13:17,177 --> 00:13:18,178
Ah!

250
00:13:19,722 --> 00:13:20,723
Ha!

251
00:13:21,557 --> 00:13:22,558
Yah!

252
00:13:22,766 --> 00:13:23,851
Ah.

253
00:13:25,477 --> 00:13:26,854
( GRUNTS )

254
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:34,194
( SNIFFLES )

255
00:13:34,278 --> 00:13:37,031
Picking fights
on your second day?

256
00:13:37,114 --> 00:13:39,408
We need to have a conference
to discuss your punishment.

257
00:13:39,491 --> 00:13:41,201
Bring your parents
to my office after school.

258
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:43,412
Parents, but...

259
00:13:43,537 --> 00:13:44,663
Don't be late.

260
00:13:53,881 --> 00:13:56,008
Thank you for coming

261
00:13:56,091 --> 00:13:57,092
Mr. And Mrs...

262
00:13:57,176 --> 00:13:59,762
Fire... Wang Fire.

263
00:13:59,845 --> 00:14:02,222
This is my wife,
Sapphire.

264
00:14:02,306 --> 00:14:04,183
Sapphire Fire,
nice to meet you.

265
00:14:04,391 --> 00:14:06,894
Mr. And Mrs. Fire...

266
00:14:06,977 --> 00:14:09,063
Your son has been enrolled
here for two days

267
00:14:09,146 --> 00:14:10,939
and he's already
causing problems.

268
00:14:11,023 --> 00:14:12,316
He's argued with
his history teacher

269
00:14:12,399 --> 00:14:14,068
disrupted music class

270
00:14:14,151 --> 00:14:15,819
and roughed up my star pupil.

271
00:14:16,111 --> 00:14:17,571
My goodness.

272
00:14:17,654 --> 00:14:19,156
That doesn't sound
like our Kuzon.

273
00:14:19,448 --> 00:14:21,200
That's what any mother
would say, ma'am.

274
00:14:21,283 --> 00:14:23,243
Nonetheless,
you're forewarned.

275
00:14:23,327 --> 00:14:25,245
If he acts up
one more time

276
00:14:25,329 --> 00:14:27,331
I'll have him sent
to reform school...

277
00:14:27,414 --> 00:14:30,042
By which I mean the coal mines.

278
00:14:30,125 --> 00:14:31,168
Are we clear?

279
00:14:31,418 --> 00:14:33,629
Don't you worry,
Mr. Headmaster

280
00:14:33,712 --> 00:14:36,465
I'll straighten this boy
out something fierce.

281
00:14:36,548 --> 00:14:37,758
Young man, as son as we get home,

282
00:14:37,841 --> 00:14:40,010
you're gonna get the punishment of
a lifetime.

283
00:14:40,094 --> 00:14:42,471
That's what I like to hear.

284
00:14:48,185 --> 00:14:50,938
MAI: Orange is such
an awful color.

285
00:14:51,021 --> 00:14:52,606
( SNICKERS )

286
00:14:52,689 --> 00:14:54,900
You're so beautiful
when you hate the world.

287
00:14:54,983 --> 00:14:56,110
I don't hate you.

288
00:14:56,193 --> 00:14:58,904
I don't hate you, too.

289
00:14:59,196 --> 00:15:01,115
( AZULA CLEARS THROAT )

290
00:15:01,365 --> 00:15:04,118
Zuko, could I have
a word with you?

291
00:15:04,201 --> 00:15:07,287
Can't you see we're busy?

292
00:15:07,371 --> 00:15:11,750
Oh, Mai, Ty Lee needs your help
untangling her braid.

293
00:15:11,834 --> 00:15:14,128
Sounds pretty serious.

294
00:15:19,925 --> 00:15:23,846
So I hear you've been to visit your
Uncle Fatso in the prison tower.

295
00:15:24,096 --> 00:15:26,181
That guard told you.

296
00:15:26,265 --> 00:15:29,184
No, you did... Just now.

297
00:15:29,393 --> 00:15:32,271
OK, you caught me.

298
00:15:32,354 --> 00:15:34,106
What is it that
you want, Azula.

299
00:15:34,189 --> 00:15:36,483
Actually, nothing.

300
00:15:36,567 --> 00:15:39,528
Believe it or not,
I'm looking out for you.

301
00:15:39,611 --> 00:15:41,655
If people find out
you've been to see Uncle

302
00:15:41,738 --> 00:15:44,241
they'll think you're
plotting with him.

303
00:15:44,324 --> 00:15:47,453
Just be careful dum-dum.

304
00:15:49,913 --> 00:15:51,665
( BIRDS SQUAWK )

305
00:15:51,748 --> 00:15:52,791
That settles it.

306
00:15:52,875 --> 00:15:54,835
No more school for you,
young man.

307
00:15:54,918 --> 00:15:55,919
AANG: I'm not
ready to leave.

308
00:15:56,378 --> 00:15:58,213
I'm having fun for once

309
00:15:58,297 --> 00:16:00,132
Just being a normal kid.

310
00:16:00,215 --> 00:16:02,468
You don't know
what it's like, Sokka.

311
00:16:02,551 --> 00:16:04,052
You get to be normal
all the time.

312
00:16:04,261 --> 00:16:06,472
Ha, ha.

313
00:16:06,555 --> 00:16:09,516
Listen, guys, those kids at school are
the future of the Fire Nation.

314
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,894
If we wanna change
this place for the better

315
00:16:12,102 --> 00:16:14,438
We need to show them
a little taste of freedom.

316
00:16:14,521 --> 00:16:18,358
What could you possibly do for a country
of depraved little fire monsters?

317
00:16:18,442 --> 00:16:21,320
I'm gonna throw them
a secret dance party.

318
00:16:21,403 --> 00:16:23,780
Go to your room.

319
00:16:34,082 --> 00:16:36,627
I can't believe we're
having a dance party.

320
00:16:36,752 --> 00:16:38,253
It seems so... Silly.

321
00:16:38,378 --> 00:16:40,506
Don't think of it
as a dance party

322
00:16:40,631 --> 00:16:43,842
But as a cultural event
celebrating the art of fancy footwork.

323
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:47,346
They're coming.

324
00:16:47,471 --> 00:16:49,640
Everyone stop bending.

325
00:16:49,765 --> 00:16:51,475
AANG: Sorry, buddy.

326
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:53,769
You should probably
wait out back.

327
00:16:53,894 --> 00:16:56,188
( GROWLS )

328
00:16:56,313 --> 00:16:59,066
AANG: I know, you've got
fancier feet than anybody...

329
00:16:59,191 --> 00:17:00,984
And six of 'em.

330
00:17:04,988 --> 00:17:07,366
( MUSIC PLAYS )

331
00:17:09,576 --> 00:17:11,828
AANG: Ladies and gentlemen.

332
00:17:11,954 --> 00:17:14,498
The Flamey-Os!

333
00:17:14,623 --> 00:17:18,001
Yeah, this ought to get
everybody moving.

334
00:17:20,504 --> 00:17:23,131
Now what
do we do?

335
00:17:23,257 --> 00:17:25,342
This is when you start dancing.

336
00:17:25,467 --> 00:17:28,762
I don't think my parents want me
dancing in a cave.

337
00:17:28,887 --> 00:17:32,349
Yeah, what if someone
finds out?

338
00:17:32,516 --> 00:17:33,600
Oh, boy.

339
00:17:33,725 --> 00:17:34,977
Listen, guys...

340
00:17:35,102 --> 00:17:37,312
Dancing isn't something
you think about.

341
00:17:37,437 --> 00:17:39,147
It's a form of self-expression

342
00:17:39,273 --> 00:17:41,483
that no one can ever
take away from you.

343
00:17:41,608 --> 00:17:45,195
Maybe it was different in the colonies,
Kuzon, but we don't do that here.

344
00:17:45,279 --> 00:17:46,280
Sure you do.

345
00:17:46,363 --> 00:17:48,740
You have for generations.

346
00:17:48,865 --> 00:17:51,618
It just so happens that I know
several classic Fire Nation dances.

347
00:17:51,743 --> 00:17:53,662
A hundred years ago

348
00:17:53,787 --> 00:17:55,122
this was known as
"The Phoenix Flight."

349
00:17:55,247 --> 00:17:57,374
STUDENTS: Ooh... Wow.

350
00:17:57,499 --> 00:18:00,502
And this was
the "Camelephant Strut".

351
00:18:03,338 --> 00:18:05,299
( GIGGLING )

352
00:18:07,884 --> 00:18:09,011
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

353
00:18:09,136 --> 00:18:12,222
Who knew Twinkle Toes
could dance?

354
00:18:12,347 --> 00:18:13,724
( CHEERING CONTINUES )

355
00:18:15,559 --> 00:18:17,978
I brought you some
komodo-chicken.

356
00:18:18,103 --> 00:18:19,688
I know you don't care for it

357
00:18:19,813 --> 00:18:22,065
but I figure
it beats prison food.

358
00:18:22,190 --> 00:18:23,317
I admit it.

359
00:18:23,442 --> 00:18:25,694
I have everything
I always wanted

360
00:18:25,819 --> 00:18:28,030
but it's not at all how
I thought it would be.

361
00:18:28,155 --> 00:18:30,574
The truth is

362
00:18:30,699 --> 00:18:32,784
I need your advice.

363
00:18:32,909 --> 00:18:35,996
I think the Avatar
is still alive.

364
00:18:36,121 --> 00:18:37,956
I know he's out there.

365
00:18:38,081 --> 00:18:40,792
I'm losing my mind.

366
00:18:40,917 --> 00:18:44,004
Please, Uncle, I'm so confused,
I need your help.

367
00:18:46,173 --> 00:18:47,507
Forget it.

368
00:18:47,633 --> 00:18:48,884
I'll solve this myself.

369
00:18:49,009 --> 00:18:50,927
Waste away in here
for all I care.

370
00:18:55,557 --> 00:18:57,392
( DOOR CREAKS SHUT )

371
00:19:01,938 --> 00:19:04,775
( DANCE MUSIC CONTINUES )

372
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:07,694
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

373
00:19:09,404 --> 00:19:11,573
And this is how they do it in
the ballrooms of Ba Sing Se.

374
00:19:18,497 --> 00:19:20,499
Wow, they look pretty
good together.

375
00:19:20,624 --> 00:19:23,293
Eh, if that's what you like.

376
00:19:25,170 --> 00:19:26,254
AANG: Yeah, that's it.

377
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:29,257
That's the sound of happy feet.

378
00:19:33,679 --> 00:19:35,138
All right, go with that.

379
00:19:35,263 --> 00:19:36,973
Everybody, freestyle.

380
00:19:54,366 --> 00:19:55,826
I don't know, Aang.

381
00:19:55,951 --> 00:19:58,036
These shoes aren't
really right for dancing

382
00:19:58,161 --> 00:20:00,205
and I'm not sure
that I know how to...

383
00:20:00,330 --> 00:20:01,331
Take my hand.

384
00:20:01,665 --> 00:20:02,791
OK.

385
00:20:24,062 --> 00:20:25,897
Aang, everyone's watching.

386
00:20:26,022 --> 00:20:27,232
Don't worry about them.

387
00:20:27,357 --> 00:20:29,860
It's just you and me right now.

388
00:20:54,801 --> 00:20:56,386
( STUDENTS GASP )

389
00:20:56,511 --> 00:20:58,221
STUDENT: Wow.

390
00:21:07,939 --> 00:21:09,441
-( MUSIC ENDS )
-( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

391
00:21:09,566 --> 00:21:12,027
( PANTING )

392
00:21:12,152 --> 00:21:13,320
( FAINT CHEERING )

393
00:21:13,445 --> 00:21:16,281
It is a dancing party.

394
00:21:16,406 --> 00:21:18,492
You did the right thing by
telling me, Hide.

395
00:21:18,617 --> 00:21:20,118
Anytime,
Headmaster, sir.

396
00:21:21,578 --> 00:21:23,663
This is incredible.

397
00:21:23,789 --> 00:21:25,957
It's like my inhibitions
just disappear.

398
00:21:31,129 --> 00:21:34,216
OK, they're back again.

399
00:21:34,341 --> 00:21:35,342
HEADMASTER: He's
the one we want.

400
00:21:35,550 --> 00:21:38,428
The boy with the headband.

401
00:21:38,553 --> 00:21:39,554
Uh-oh.

402
00:21:45,018 --> 00:21:46,061
GUARD: Got ya.

403
00:21:46,186 --> 00:21:47,395
Looking for me?

404
00:21:49,064 --> 00:21:50,440
That's not the one.

405
00:21:50,565 --> 00:21:52,150
He's here somewhere.

406
00:21:52,275 --> 00:21:53,443
Don't let him leave the cave.

407
00:21:58,532 --> 00:21:59,533
Yes?

408
00:22:04,287 --> 00:22:05,914
- Hi there.
- How we doing?

409
00:22:13,255 --> 00:22:14,256
Looking for someone?

410
00:22:16,424 --> 00:22:17,509
Who are you
looking for?

411
00:22:17,592 --> 00:22:18,885
Do you need something?

412
00:22:19,010 --> 00:22:20,011
Over here.

413
00:22:33,608 --> 00:22:36,528
Stop that.

414
00:22:36,653 --> 00:22:37,654
Stop that.

415
00:22:40,407 --> 00:22:42,367
We're safe, Sokka.

416
00:22:42,450 --> 00:22:43,994
You can take off
the mustache, now.

417
00:22:44,077 --> 00:22:45,829
Oh, no, I can't.

418
00:22:45,912 --> 00:22:48,290
It's permanently
glued to my skin.

419
00:22:48,373 --> 00:22:50,750
Way to go, dancy pants.

420
00:22:50,834 --> 00:22:53,086
I think you really
did help those kids.

421
00:22:53,211 --> 00:22:54,588
You taught them to be free.

422
00:22:54,671 --> 00:22:55,672
I don't know.

423
00:22:55,755 --> 00:22:57,632
It was just
a dance party, that's all.

424
00:22:57,716 --> 00:23:00,218
Well, that was some
dance party, Aang.

425
00:23:00,844 --> 00:23:02,137
Mwah.

426
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:04,973
Flamey-O, sir...

427
00:23:05,098 --> 00:23:06,808
Flamey-O.

428
00:23:12,522 --> 00:23:15,400
( BIRDS CAWING )

429
00:23:17,485 --> 00:23:18,862
( GATE OPENS )

430
00:23:20,864 --> 00:23:22,490
You're sure
you weren't followed?

431
00:23:22,616 --> 00:23:24,784
ZUKO: I've heard about you.

432
00:23:24,910 --> 00:23:27,120
They say you're good
at what you do

433
00:23:27,245 --> 00:23:29,539
and even better
at keeping secrets.

434
00:23:29,664 --> 00:23:31,958
The Avatar's alive.

435
00:23:32,083 --> 00:23:34,169
I want you to find him

436
00:23:34,294 --> 00:23:36,046
and end him.

437
00:23:49,392 --> 00:23:53,229
( ♪... )
